{"tool_name":"scar","contents":["oeb","bioschemas","biotools"],"fetched_metadata":{"biotools":{"id":"scar","home":"http://8.142.154.29/SCAR2023","license":"CC-BY-4.0","summary":"Single-cell and spatially-resolved cancer resources.","addition_date":"2024-03-18T15:15:33.062562Z","last_update_date":"2024-11-24T14:08:36.274585Z","tool_type":["Database portal"],"biotools_curie":"biotools:scar","cost":"Free of charge","credit":[{"email":"li-huang19@mails.tsinghua.edu.cn","name":"Li Huang","typeEntity":"Person"},{"email":"xdwang@fuccb.com","name":"Xiangdong Wang","typeEntity":"Person"},{"name":"Dongsheng Chen","orcidid":"https://orcid.org/0000-0002-7196-4136","typeEntity":"Person"}],"edit_permission":{"type":"private"},"function":[{"operation":[{"term":"Essential dynamics","uri":"http://edamontology.org/operation_3891"},{"term":"Gene expression profiling","uri":"http://edamontology.org/operation_0314"},{"term":"Visualisation","uri":"http://edamontology.org/operation_0337"}]}],"name":"SCAR","operating_system":["Linux","Mac","Windows"],"owner":"Pub2Tools","publication":[{"doi":"10.1093/nar/gkad753","metadata":{"abstract":"A dv ances in sequencing and imaging technologies offer a unique opportunity to unra v el cell heterogeneity and de v elop ne w immunotherap y strategies for cancer research. There is an urgent need for a resource that effectively integrates a vast amount of transcriptomic profiling data to comprehensively explore cancer tissue heterogeneity and the tumor microenvironment. In this conte xt, w e de v eloped the Single-cell and Spatially -resolv ed Cancer R esources (SCAR) database, a combined tumor spatial and single-cell transcriptomic platform, which is freely accessible at ht tp://8.1 42.1 54.29/SCAR2023 or ht tp://scaratlas.com . SCAR contains spatial transcriptomic data from 21 tumor tissues and single- cell transcriptomic data from 11 301 352 cells encompassing 395 cancer subtypes and co v ering a wide variety of tissues, organoids, and cell lines. This resource offers diverse functional modules to address k e y cancer research questions at multiple le v els, including the screening of tumor cell t ypes, met abolic features, cell communication and gene expression patterns within the tumor microen vironment. Moreo v er, SCAR enables the analysis of biomarker expression patterns and cell developmental trajectories. SCAR also provides a comprehensive analysis of multi-dimensional datasets based on 34 state-of-the-art omics techniques, serving as an essential tool for in-depth mining and understanding of cell heterogeneity and spatial location. The implications of this resource extend to both cancer biology research and cancer immunotherapy de v elopment.","authors":[{"name":"Chang A."},{"name":"Chen D."},{"name":"Chen P."},{"name":"Deng Y."},{"name":"Huang L."},{"name":"Jia T."},{"name":"Li C."},{"name":"Li M."},{"name":"Liu H."},{"name":"Qin S."},{"name":"Shen J."},{"name":"Wang X."},{"name":"Xiao J."},{"name":"Xue R."},{"name":"Zhang N."},{"name":"Zhang W."}],"citationCount":4,"date":"2024-01-05T00:00:00Z","journal":"Nucleic Acids Research","title":"SCAR: Single-cell and Spatially -r esolved Cancer Resources"},"pmcid":"PMC10767865","pmid":"37739405"}],"topic":[{"term":"Biomarkers","uri":"http://edamontology.org/topic_3360"},{"term":"Immunology","uri":"http://edamontology.org/topic_0804"},{"term":"Metabolomics","uri":"http://edamontology.org/topic_3172"},{"term":"Oncology","uri":"http://edamontology.org/topic_2640"},{"term":"Transcriptomics","uri":"http://edamontology.org/topic_3308"}]},"bioschemas":{"name":"SCAR","home":"https://bio.tools/scar","license":"CC-BY-4.0","summary":"Single-cell and spatially-resolved cancer resources.","tool_type":"sc:SoftwareApplication"},"oeb":{"metrics":[{"@id":"https://openebench.bsc.es/monitor/metrics/biotools:scar/db/8.142.154.29","@license":"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/","@nmsp":"biotools","@type":"metrics","deprecated":true,"distribution":{"sourcecode":{"interpre